# Environment — all env files are local to your machine and never committed
# (the dev API URL is usually your own LAN IP, which changes per network). Create
# `.env.development`, `.env.staging` and `.env.production` by copying
# `.env.example`; the android:*/ios:*/start:* scripts pick one via APP_ENV.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.staging
.env.production

